WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.000
Hey, what's the matter with you?

00:02.000 --> 00:03.000
You got the wrong place.

00:25.000 --> 00:27.000
Hey, what's the matter with you?

00:27.000 --> 00:31.000
Hey, that's a good shooting, little Jim.

00:31.000 --> 00:34.000
Cleanest back shot I've ever seen in my life.

00:34.000 --> 00:36.000
Call for another one.

00:36.000 --> 00:39.000
Hey, what's the matter with you?

00:54.000 --> 00:57.000
That's a shame. He had a full house.

01:00.000 --> 01:02.000
You can't win them all.

01:02.000 --> 01:05.000
Drink's on him.

01:09.000 --> 01:12.000
Them's the meanest, toughest killers I ever saw.

01:12.000 --> 01:13.000
Who are they?

01:13.000 --> 01:16.000
Well, them's the Slade boys. Didn't you know that?

01:16.000 --> 01:17.000
No.

01:17.000 --> 01:19.000
Well, sure lucky they didn't plug us, too.

01:19.000 --> 01:21.000
The Slade boys.

01:21.000 --> 01:23.000
I'm sure glad they're riding on through.

01:23.000 --> 01:25.000
Do you know where they're heading?

01:25.000 --> 01:28.000
I heard them mention a place called Kewa Flats.

01:28.000 --> 01:31.000
Slade boys. Kewa Flats.

01:31.000 --> 01:34.000
Remind me to ride clear of that place, will you?

01:34.000 --> 01:35.000
Come on, give me a drink.

01:35.000 --> 01:36.000
Yeah.

01:52.000 --> 01:54.000
Sheriff! Sheriff!

01:54.000 --> 01:55.000
What is it?

01:55.000 --> 01:58.000
They're coming. I seen them up by the forks, Mr. Brown.

01:58.000 --> 02:00.000
Woodham's about nine foot tall.

02:00.000 --> 02:02.000
Well, who'll come and...

02:02.000 --> 02:03.000
Them!

02:03.000 --> 02:05.000
You say one of them's a big, tall man?

02:05.000 --> 02:08.000
About nine foot tall and half as big around.

02:08.000 --> 02:10.000
And the other fella is a little bit of a fella?

02:10.000 --> 02:12.000
About half as big as his brother.

02:13.000 --> 02:15.000
And mean looking?

02:15.000 --> 02:17.000
Meaner than rattlesnakes.

02:17.000 --> 02:19.000
It's them, all right. It's them.

02:19.000 --> 02:21.000
Now, Sonny, you get in off the street.

02:21.000 --> 02:22.000
Get in the house, you hear me?

02:22.000 --> 02:24.000
Keep off the streets.

02:24.000 --> 02:31.000
Now, go on, get.

02:31.000 --> 02:33.000
I...

02:33.000 --> 02:36.000
Ain't no sense looking for trouble.

02:36.000 --> 02:39.000
Durn thing never was no good know-how.

02:43.000 --> 02:45.000
They're coming!

02:49.000 --> 02:50.000
They're coming!

02:50.000 --> 02:52.000
They're coming.

02:52.000 --> 02:54.000
They're coming, ladies. They're coming.

02:54.000 --> 02:56.000
They're breaking through.

02:56.000 --> 02:58.000
They're coming.

02:58.000 --> 03:00.000
He's showing good sense.

03:03.000 --> 03:05.000
They're coming!

03:05.000 --> 03:15.000
They're coming.

03:15.000 --> 03:17.000
They're coming.

03:17.000 --> 03:30.000
They've come.

03:48.000 --> 03:51.000
I don't know about these stars, nothing.

03:51.000 --> 03:52.000
Hey, Oz.

03:52.000 --> 03:53.000
Yeah?

03:53.000 --> 03:55.000
Let's wash some of the trail list out.

03:55.000 --> 03:57.000
It's a good idea, little Joe.

04:01.000 --> 04:02.000
Howdy.

04:02.000 --> 04:04.000
Howdy.

04:04.000 --> 04:06.000
Howdy.

04:06.000 --> 04:23.000
Howdy.

04:23.000 --> 04:24.000
Quillibug, get up. Get up.

04:24.000 --> 04:25.000
Get up, Quillie.

04:25.000 --> 04:27.000
All right, all right, all right.

04:27.000 --> 04:29.000
Morning, Sheriff. Morning. Morning.

04:29.000 --> 04:32.000
Well, don't mind if I do. Who's by him?

04:32.000 --> 04:35.000
You're always talking about how well you knew them Slade boys.

04:35.000 --> 04:36.000
That's right. That's right.

04:36.000 --> 04:38.000
Just how well do you know them?

04:38.000 --> 04:42.000
Sheriff, me and them Slade boys was practically weaned together.

04:42.000 --> 04:44.000
I am their bosom friend.

04:44.000 --> 04:45.000
Yeah.

04:45.000 --> 04:47.000
Well, your bosom friends just rode into town.

04:47.000 --> 04:50.000
Sheriff, well, uh...

04:50.000 --> 04:52.000
Yeah, yeah, yeah. All right.

04:58.000 --> 05:00.000
Say that again.

05:00.000 --> 05:03.000
Your bosom friends just rode into town.

05:03.000 --> 05:08.000
Well, why would those two murderous villains want to come to a miserable hole like Keowa Flats?

05:08.000 --> 05:11.000
Because Alonzo McFadden hired them to kill off all the Hadfield boys.

05:11.000 --> 05:12.000
That's why.

05:12.000 --> 05:13.000
Oh, that's right.

05:13.000 --> 05:15.000
Well, where are they now?

05:15.000 --> 05:16.000
In the bar.

05:16.000 --> 05:18.000
Oh, no. That's terrible.

05:18.000 --> 05:20.000
No, Sheriff, that's the only bar in town.

05:20.000 --> 05:22.000
Never mind. Never mind.

05:22.000 --> 05:23.000
What do you mean, never mind?

05:23.000 --> 05:24.000
You listen to me. You ruined...

05:24.000 --> 05:25.000
All right. All right.

05:25.000 --> 05:26.000
Oh, you go to the delivery stable.

05:26.000 --> 05:27.000
Get a horse. Hire it.

05:27.000 --> 05:30.000
Charge it to me and ride out and tell old Jubal Hadfield

05:30.000 --> 05:33.000
not to come into town for quite a spell.

05:33.000 --> 05:35.000
Then when you come back, look me up,

05:35.000 --> 05:37.000
because I'll need you to identify them two fellows.

05:37.000 --> 05:38.000
All right. I'll do it right away.

05:38.000 --> 05:39.000
Now, look, look, look.

05:39.000 --> 05:41.000
Look after the bar.

05:41.000 --> 05:42.000
Will you look after it?

05:42.000 --> 05:43.000
Yeah, I will.

05:48.000 --> 05:49.000
Hey, little Joe.

05:49.000 --> 05:51.000
There's something wrong with me.

05:51.000 --> 05:52.000
Do I smell or something?

05:54.000 --> 05:55.000
No, you smell about the same.

05:55.000 --> 05:56.000
How about me?

05:58.000 --> 05:59.000
About the same.

05:59.000 --> 06:00.000
About the same.

06:04.000 --> 06:05.000
Say, mister.

06:06.000 --> 06:07.000
Yes, yes, sir?

06:08.000 --> 06:10.000
Is there something wrong with us or something?

06:10.0